From: Hunter Laux <hunterlaux@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] serialposix: set custom baud rates on MIPS

pyserial 3.5 always uses the asm-generic TCGETS2/TCSETS2 numbers. MIPS
encodes ioctl directions differently, so the kernel rejects them with
ENOTTY and every baud rate outside the termios table fails, including
Klipper's default of 250000.

MIPS also has NCCS 23, so struct termios2 is 48 bytes and c_ispeed and
c_ospeed are words 10 and 11, not 9 and 10. Changing only the ioctl
numbers writes the rate into the end of c_cc and c_ispeed and leaves
c_ospeed at the BOTHER placeholder: the port then sends at 4096 baud.

Backported from pyserial master (5ce1773f, 2aea0ba4); there is no
pyserial release after 3.5.

Upstream: https://github.com/pyserial/pyserial/commit/5ce1773f
Signed-off-by: Hunter Laux <hunterlaux@gmail.com>
---
--- a/serial/serialposix.py
+++ b/serial/serialposix.py
@@ -32,6 +32,7 @@
 import errno
 import fcntl
 import os
+import platform
 import select
 import struct
 import sys
@@ -80,8 +81,16 @@
     CMSPAR = 0o10000000000  # Use "stick" (mark/space) parity
 
     # baudrate ioctls
-    TCGETS2 = 0x802C542A
-    TCSETS2 = 0x402C542B
+    if platform.machine().startswith('mips'):
+        # MIPS encodes ioctl directions differently and has a larger
+        # struct termios2 (NCCS is 23), so the speeds sit one word later
+        TCGETS2 = 0x4030542A
+        TCSETS2 = 0x8030542B
+        BAUDRATE_OFFSET = 10
+    else:
+        TCGETS2 = 0x802C542A
+        TCSETS2 = 0x402C542B
+        BAUDRATE_OFFSET = 9
     BOTHER = 0o010000
 
     # RS485 ioctls
@@ -154,7 +163,7 @@
                 # set custom speed
                 buf[2] &= ~termios.CBAUD
                 buf[2] |= BOTHER
-                buf[9] = buf[10] = baudrate
+                buf[BAUDRATE_OFFSET] = buf[BAUDRATE_OFFSET + 1] = baudrate
 
                 # set serial_struct
                 fcntl.ioctl(self.fd, TCSETS2, buf)
